<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $4.8 mln Dec 16.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $4.8 mln Dec 16.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $4.8 million deficit on December 16 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON DECEMBER 16</p>
<p>Exports: $219.7 million</p>
<p>Imports: $189.6 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $286.1 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $321 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $4.8 million</p>
<p>DECEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.212 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.212 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.787 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.767 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.020 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2485418</p>
